# Cloud sync (optional).
#
# Leave these unset and the app still works completely: IndexedDB is the source
# of truth, and the Settings screen simply reports that sync is not configured
# for this build. Nothing here is loaded until someone signs in.
#
# The publishable key is safe to ship in a client bundle. It grants nothing on
# its own — every table is behind row-level security, and every policy is
# written against auth.uid(). It lives here rather than in source so that a
# fork points at its own Supabase project instead of silently at this one.
#
# Find both under Project Settings -> API. Use the sb_publishable_... key, not
# the legacy anon JWT and never the service_role key, which bypasses RLS and
# must never reach a browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Only needed to run `npm run test:sync`, the end-to-end check against a live
# project. See the comment at the top of scripts/sync-e2e.ts for the SQL that
# creates the two throwaway accounts it signs in as. Never point this at a
# project holding real data — the script clears the account before each run.
E2E_PASSWORD=
